{
  "id": "association_history_and_replay",
  "title": "Ordered content and membership histories keep independent validity and observation bounds across backfill, equal-successor coalescing, ownership movement and WAL replay",
  "obligations": [
    "fixed-case-4",
    "fixed-case-8",
    "gap-info-band-execution",
    "invariant-11",
    "invariant-5",
    "invariant-6",
    "route-metadata-http",
    "route-promql-info"
  ],
  "routes": [
    "columnar"
  ],
  "open_decisions": [
    "9"
  ],
  "scope": "Settled decision-2 history semantics only. Effective time defines order; the fixture commits a forward A/B/A sequence and then backfills an observation inside the first A epoch and an actual B change point equal to its immediate successor. The retained history is A [1000,1800), B [1800,3000), A [3000,inf): the late B observation coalesces the redundant change point at 2000 while preserving both observation ranges, and observation bounds never become validity bounds. A Scrape owner history changes at 2500 outside the series' Scrape membership band [1200,2200), proving content and membership histories are independent. The fixture exercises no explicit clear or association termination: decision 3 (2026-11-15) accepts those semantics, but the incumbent cannot represent them and they remain target cases. It states no unresolved-association retention and exercises no acquisition or reconciliation path; decision 4 (2026-11-15) is decided and the incumbent implements neither side of it. Decision 5 (2026-11-15) is decided too, but this fixture keeps using an opaque Scrape content string and claims no provenance role, component, completeness or trust semantics. PR99 grammar is decision 6 (2026-11-18): accepted, but the incumbent has no native reference syntax and this fixture exercises none. Snapshot cursors are decision 7 (2026-11-19); admission budgets (9) remain open. Replay is asserted from the same committed log after reopening the store, not as a commutativity claim for unrelated commit orders.",
